  "encounterTable": "route_2",
  "_design": "Four shelves rising north out of Briarbell, each closed by a two-row rock band with exactly one pass through it, and the passes deliberately not above one another -- so the road zigzags the whole width of the map to find them: north, east, north, west, north. Ledges are the way back down and only work that way. The three branches hang off the road rather than lying along it: the tarn west of shelf 1 (Wade), the thorn alcove east of shelf 1 (Clear), the cave west of shelf 2 (Shoulder, inside it). THE ARCH IS NOT A BRANCH. The road runs straight across its apron, because it is the first story beat of the game and is not allowed to be optional.",
  "_plan": "The first real forest. Canopy goes down as overlapping discs rather than as a per-tile probability, because a probability gives evenly spaced trunks on a lawn and a wood is clumps with holes between them; the road is laid last so nothing can grow across it. The bands read as terraces rather than walls because the north row of each carries the turf lip of the shelf above -- 'c' on top, 'C' underneath, which is the way round the tileset draws them -- and because only the stretches carrying a pass, a ledge or the arch are rock at all. The rest of every terrace is a wall of trees. The thorn on the east spur is one season old and three people on this route say so.",
